
# Use bd merge for beads JSONL files
.beads/beads.jsonl merge=beads

# Every PR appends a line under the same `### <date>` heading in the changelog,
# so every pair of open PRs conflicts there and nowhere else — eight times in one
# session (#661). `union` is git's built-in "keep both sides" driver, which is
# exactly the resolution a human performs by hand each time. It leaves how
# entries are written untouched; the append-within-day vs. file-per-entry
# convention question stays open on #661.
#
# Proven by scripts/test_changelog_merge.py, which runs the two-branch case in a
# temp repo against this file — delete the line below and that test fails.
docs/CHANGELOG.md merge=union
